\name{density_multipliers}
\alias{density_multipliers}
\alias{ceiling_density_multiplier}
\alias{beverton_holt_multiplier}
\alias{ricker_multiplier}
\title{Density-feedback multipliers}
\usage{
ceiling_density_multiplier(n, capacity)

beverton_holt_multiplier(n, capacity, growth)

ricker_multiplier(n, capacity, growth)
}
\arguments{
\item{n}{Number of living individuals (or any abundance the feedback acts on).}
\item{capacity}{Abundance at which the feedback reaches its reference strength.}
\item{growth}{Low-density growth multiplier (at least 1) that the feedback offsets at capacity.}
}
\description{
Multipliers in (0, 1] for a vital rate. \code{ceiling_density_multiplier()} is 1 up to capacity and \code{capacity / n} above it. \code{beverton_holt_multiplier()} is \code{1 / (1 + (growth - 1) n / capacity)} and \code{ricker_multiplier()} is \code{growth^(-n / capacity)}; both equal \code{1 / growth} at capacity, so a rate that supports growth \code{growth} at low density gives zero growth at capacity.
}
\value{
A numeric vector of multipliers.
}
\examples{
n <- c(0, 50, 100, 200)
beverton_holt_multiplier(n, capacity = 100, growth = 1.5)
ricker_multiplier(n, capacity = 100, growth = 1.5)
ceiling_density_multiplier(n, capacity = 100)
}
